        "Eugene S. Polzik",
        "H. Jeff Kimble",
        "Mikhail D. Lukin"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Light-matter quantum interfaces are a foundational enabling technology for quantum networks, connecting propagating photons to long-lived matter systems.",
        "attribution": "Polzik, Kimble, and Lukin made distinct and influential experimental contributions to the principal interface architectures.",
        "maturity": "Individual memories and interfaces are convincingly demonstrated, with rapid technical progress across platforms.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "A fully scalable fault-tolerant quantum network is not yet realized.",
          "Credit is diffuse across several physical platforms and many key groups."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 8,
